    <div class="mb-8">
      <h2 class="text-gray-400 text-lg mb-4">//projects</h2>
      <div class="grid grid-cols-2 gap-4">
        <div class="project-card border border-gray-600 px-4 py-3 rounded bg-gray-800 cursor-pointer hover:bg-gray-700 hover:border-gray-500 transition-all duration-300 ease-in-out transform hover:-translate-y-1" data-project="domain-scout">
          <div class="font-semibold text-lg">Domain Scout</div>
          <div class="text-gray-400 text-sm mb-2">//Python, SQL</div>
          <p class="text-sm">identifies disposable email addresses used as contact methods in WHOIS records for Domain Control Validation</p>
          
          <!-- Expanded content (hidden by default) -->
          <div class="project-details hidden mt-4 pt-4">
            <div class="space-y-3">
              <div>
                <h4 class="font-semibold text-emerald-400 mb-2">What it does:</h4>
                <p class="text-sm text-gray-300">Domain Scout is the primary GUI to view vulnerable domains found by Domain Scout API. Domain Scout API identifies disposable email addresses used as contact methods in WHOIS records. Domains are collected using Certstream Server Go which streams Certificate Transparency logs continuously to a websocket connection. Domains are extracted from the data stream and WHOIS queries are subsequently made to identify contact email addresses which are compared against a list of 15k+ known disposable email domains. If a disposable email address is found, the domain and associated data is added to the database and displayed in Domain Scout.</p>
              </div>
              <div>
                <h4 class="font-semibold text-emerald-400 mb-2">Key Features:</h4>
                <ul class="text-sm text-gray-300 list-disc list-inside space-y-1">
                  <li>TLS certificate transparency log parsing and analysis</li>
                  <li>Disposable email detection algorithms</li>
                  <li>SQL database for storing results</li>
                  <li>Batch processing capabilities</li>
                </ul>
              </div>
              <div class="flex space-x-3">
                <a href="https://github.com/derekrgreene/Domain-Scout" class="text-blue-400 hover:text-blue-300 text-sm transition-colors">🔗 GitHub</a>
                <a href="/Domain_Scout_README.md" class="text-blue-400 hover:text-blue-300 text-sm transition-colors">📖 README</a>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="project-card border border-gray-600 px-4 py-3 rounded bg-gray-800 cursor-pointer hover:bg-gray-700 transition-colors" data-project="small-shell">
          <div class="font-semibold text-lg">Small Shell</div>
          <div class="text-gray-400 text-sm mb-2">//C</div>
          <p class="text-sm">simple shell that can run commands in the foreground and background, with input and output redirection</p>
          
          <!-- Expanded content -->
          <div class="project-details hidden mt-4 pt-4">
            <div class="space-y-3">
              <div>
                <h4 class="font-semibold text-emerald-400 mb-2">What it does:</h4>
                <p class="text-sm text-gray-300">This program implements a simple shell that can run commands in the foreground and background, with input and output redirection. It also handles built-in commands such as exit, cd, and status. Signals such as SIGINT, SIGCHLD, and SIGTSTP are handled as well. Comments can be added to the input by starting the line with '#'. Blank lines are ignored. The '&' character can be used to run a command in the background. Program will terminate upon 'exit' command.</p>
              </div>
              <div>
                <h4 class="font-semibold text-emerald-400 mb-2">Key Features:</h4>
                <ul class="text-sm text-gray-300 list-disc list-inside space-y-1">
                  <li>Command execution in foreground/background</li>
                  <li>Input/output redirection (&gt;, &lt;, &gt;&gt;)</li>
                  <li>Process management and job control</li>
                  <li>Built-in commands (cd, exit, jobs)</li>
                </ul>
              </div>
              <div class="flex space-x-3">
                <a href="https://github.com/derekrgreene/derekrgreene.com/blob/master/static/sources/src/smallsh.c" class="text-blue-400 hover:text-blue-300 text-sm transition-colors">🔗 GitHub</a>
                <a href="/Small_shell_README.md" class="text-blue-400 hover:text-blue-300 text-sm transition-colors">📖 README</a>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="project-card border border-gray-600 px-4 py-3 rounded bg-gray-800 cursor-pointer hover:bg-gray-700 hover:text-white transition-colors" data-project="low-level-io">
          <div class="font-semibold text-lg">Low Level IO</div>
          <div class="text-gray-400 text-sm mb-2">//x86 MASM</div>
          <p class="text-sm">low level IO interface designed in assembly</p>
          
          <!-- Expanded content -->
          <div class="project-details hidden mt-4 pt-4">
            <div class="space-y-3">
              <div>
                <h4 class="font-semibold text-emerald-400 mb-2">What it does:</h4>
                <p class="text-sm text-gray-300">Program displays title and programmers name, followed by an introduction explaining the program. Program then prompts user to enter 10 signed decimal integers in range of 32 bits/number. Input is read in as a string and converted from ASCII to decimal. Each input is then checked for if it is valid. If it is not valid, the program will display an error message and prompt the user to re-enter the number. If the number is valid, it is stored in an array. The program then displays the numbers entered, followed by the sum and average for the values inputed. Results are converted to ASCII and then displayed to the user along with a list of the numbers entered. The program then displays a goodbye message and exits.</p>
              </div>
              <div>
                <h4 class="font-semibold text-emerald-400 mb-2">Key Features:</h4>
                <ul class="text-sm text-gray-300 list-disc list-inside space-y-1">
                  <li>User input validation and error handling</li>
                  <li>ASCII to decimal conversion</li>
                  <li>Array storage and management</li>
                  <li>Mathematical calculations (sum, average)</li>
                  <li>Decimal to ASCII conversion for output</li>
                  <li>Input range validation (32-bit signed integers)</li>
                </ul>
              </div>
              <div class="flex space-x-3">
                <a href="https://github.com/derekrgreene/derekrgreene.com/blob/master/static/sources/src/low-level-io.asm" class="text-blue-400 hover:text-blue-300 text-sm transition-colors">🔗 GitHub</a>
                <a href="https://www.asmirvine.com/workbook/workbook.htm" class="text-blue-400 hover:text-blue-300 text-sm transition-colors">📖 Assembly Guide</a>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

